## Assembly
The browser shows the relationships used to assemble the mechanism:

| Type | Name |
|------|------|
| Joint | Revolute 1 |
| Joint | Revolute 2 |
| Joint | Slider 4 |
| Constraint | Constraint 1 (Tangent) |
| Constraint | Constraint 2 (Tangent) |

- The revolute joints let the disc and the crank rotate about their pins.
- The slider joint lets the slider move in a straight line only.
- The tangent constraints keep the parts in contact as the mechanism moves.

