## Animation
The mechanism is animated by driving a revolute joint: the disc turns and the crank and slider follow. The screen recording shows the full motion:

[quick_return_mechanism.mp4](video/quick_return_mechanism.mp4)

## Steps
1. Sketch and model each part (base, disc, crank, slider) as its own component.
2. Place the components in the assembly.
3. Add revolute joints for the disc and the crank, and a slider joint for the slider.
4. Add tangent constraints where the parts must stay in contact.
5. Drive the revolute joint to animate the mechanism, and record it.

## Notes
- Making each part a component is what allows joints and animation. A body cannot take a joint.
- Joints decide how a part may move, so choosing the right joint (revolute for rotation, slider for straight-line motion) is the key skill in assembly.
- Driving one joint moves the rest of the mechanism, so one input shows the whole motion.
- What this task covers: modelling parts, components, joints, constraints and animation in Fusion 360.
